    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d5-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d5-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Carter Library, National Security Council, Institutional Files, Box 41,
                    Folder 3, PRM–23 [3]. Top Secret; Talent Keyhole; Comint. The meeting took place
                    in the Old Executive Office Building.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d5-f2" n="2" xml:id="d5-f2-content">
                <p>Presumably Brown is referring to a briefing memorandum on space policy issues
                    which was not found.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d5-f3" n="3" xml:id="d5-f3-content">
                <p>In a March 4 letter to Brezhnev, Carter wrote that he wanted to “reach an early
                    agreement” on a number of issues, including an “agreement not to arm satellites
                    nor to develop the ability to destroy or damage satellites.” The letter is
                    printed in full in <ref target="frus1977-80v06#d13">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations,</hi> 1977–1980, vol. VI, Soviet
                        Union, Document 13</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
